            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-27929",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Use After Free in SixLabors.ImageSharp"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "ImageSharp is a managed, cross-platform, 2D graphics library. A heap-use-after-free flaw was found in ImageSharp's InitializeImage() function of PngDecoderCore.cs file. This vulnerability is triggered when an attacker passes a specially crafted PNG image file to ImageSharp for conversion, potentially leading to information disclosure. This issue has been patched in versions 3.1.3 and 2.1.7."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-27929",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-27929\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: SixLabors.ImageSharp\nFixed Version: 3.1.3, 2.1.7\nLink: [CVE-2024-27929](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-27929)\nImageSharp is a managed, cross-platform, 2D graphics library. A heap-use-after-free flaw was found in ImageSharp's InitializeImage() function of PngDecoderCore.cs file. This vulnerability is triggered when an attacker passes a specially crafted PNG image file to ImageSharp for conversion, potentially leading to information disclosure. This issue has been patched in versions 3.1.3 and 2.1.7.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-27929**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|SixLabors.ImageSharp|3.1.3, 2.1.7|[CVE-2024-27929](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-27929)|\n\nImageSharp is a managed, cross-platform, 2D graphics library. A heap-use-after-free flaw was found in ImageSharp's InitializeImage() function of PngDecoderCore.cs file. This vulnerability is triggered when an attacker passes a specially crafted PNG image file to ImageSharp for conversion, potentially leading to information disclosure. This issue has been patched in versions 3.1.3 and 2.1.7."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.1,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H",
